We are building a Node.js/TypeScript video editing pipeline called Splicewerk. It uses ffmpeg locally, Runway for AI video generation, and Shotstack for cloud assembly.

Below are 3 key files from the pipeline. Please review them as a senior ffmpeg engineer and provide specific, actionable fixes for the known issues listed at the end.

--- src/edl/types.ts ---
Defines the TypeScript interface for a TimelineSegment — the atomic unit in our EDL (Edit Decision List). Each segment has a type, optional processor (ffmpeg/runway/elevenlabs), source file reference, trim times, and text overlay config.

export interface TimelineSegment {
  id: string;
  type: 'intro' | 'outro' | 'title_card' | 'before_after' | 'montage' | 'clip' | 'transition' | 'generated';
  processor?: 'ffmpeg' | 'runway' | 'elevenlabs';
  source?: string;
  sources?: { source: string; trim?: string }[];
  operation?: string;
  prompt?: string;
  durationSeconds?: number;
  trim?: string;
  transition?: string;
  textOverlay?: { text: string; position: string; style: string; };
}

--- src/services/ffmpeg.ts (key functions) ---
Our ffmpeg service layer. Wraps execFile calls to the local ffmpeg binary. Key functions: trimClip (trim a video segment), imageToClip (convert a still image to a video clip), generateTitleCard (currently a placeholder black clip because drawtext is unavailable — libfreetype not compiled in).

const FFMPEG_BIN = resolveFFmpegPath(); // searches /opt/homebrew/bin/ffmpeg etc

async function runFFmpeg(args: string[]): Promise<Result<string>> {
  try {
    const { stdout, stderr } = await execFileAsync(FFMPEG_BIN, args);
    return { ok: true, value: stdout };
  } catch (err) {
    const error = err as { message?: string; stderr?: string };
    return { ok: false, error: error.stderr ?? error.message ?? 'Unknown ffmpeg error' };
  }
}

export async function trimClip(input, startSec, endSec, output) {
  const args = [
    '-y',
    '-ss', String(startSec),   // fast seek BEFORE -i
    '-to', String(endSec),
    '-i', input,
    '-c:v', 'h264_videotoolbox',  // macOS hardware encoder
    '-allow_sw', '1',
    '-c:a', 'aac',
    output,
  ];
  return runFFmpeg(args);
}

export async function imageToClip(input, durationSec, output, width=1920, height=1080) {
  const args = [
    '-y', '-loop', '1', '-i', input,
    '-t', String(durationSec),
    '-vf', `scale=${width}:${height}:force_original_aspect_ratio=decrease,pad=${width}:${height}:(ow-iw)/2:(oh-ih)/2`,
    '-c:v', 'h264_videotoolbox',
    '-allow_sw', '1',
    '-pix_fmt', 'yuv420p',
    '-r', '30',
    output,
  ];
  return runFFmpeg(args);
}

export async function generateTitleCard(text, durationSec, output, width=1920, height=1080) {
  // drawtext not available — libfreetype not compiled in
  // Currently just generates a plain black clip as placeholder
  const args = [
    '-y',
    '-f', 'lavfi',
    '-i', `color=c=black:s=${width}x${height}:r=30:d=${durationSec}`,
    '-c:v', 'h264_videotoolbox',
    '-allow_sw', '1',
    '-pix_fmt', 'yuv420p',
    '-t', String(durationSec),
    output,
  ];
  return runFFmpeg(args);
}

--- src/inngest/functions/produce-video.ts (render-segments step) ---
The Inngest pipeline step that processes each EDL segment. Resolves LLM-generated filenames to actual file paths using fuzzy matching (LLM often generates wrong filenames like '0295.mp4' instead of 'IMG_0295.MOV'), then dispatches to ffmpeg or Runway based on the segment's processor field. The 'operation: stabilize' field is currently ignored with no implementation.

// Resolve LLM-generated filenames to actual paths
const assetByFilename = new Map(manifest.files.map(f => [f.filename.toLowerCase(), f.path]));
const assetByNumber = new Map(); // e.g. '0295' -> '/path/IMG_0295.MOV'
for (const f of manifest.files) {
  const nums = f.filename.match(/\d+/);
  if (nums) assetByNumber.set(nums[0], f.path);
}
const resolveSource = (source) => {
  if (source.startsWith('/')) return source;
  const exact = assetByFilename.get(source.toLowerCase());
  if (exact) return exact;
  const noExt = source.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '').toLowerCase();
  const noExtMatch = assetByFilename.get(noExt);
  if (noExtMatch) return noExtMatch;
  const nums = source.match(/\d+/);
  if (nums) { const numMatch = assetByNumber.get(nums[0]); if (numMatch) return numMatch; }
  return source; // unresolved — will fail later
};

// Per-segment processing
if (processor === 'ffmpeg' && sourcePath) {
  if (seg.trim) {
    const [startStr, endStr] = seg.trim.split('-');
    const result = await trimClip(sourcePath, parseTrimTime(startStr), parseTrimTime(endStr), outputPath);
    if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to trim segment ${seg.id}: ${result.error}`);
    results.push({ path: outputPath, durationSeconds: endSec - startSec });
  } else {
    // No trim — verify file exists and pass through
    try {
      await fs.access(sourcePath);
      results.push({ path: sourcePath, durationSeconds: seg.durationSeconds ?? 5 });
    } catch {
      console.warn(`Skipping segment ${seg.id}: file not found at ${sourcePath}`);
    }
  }
}
// operation: 'stabilize' in EDL is currently IGNORED — no implementation

Known issues to address:
1. drawtext filter not available (ffmpeg built without libfreetype) — need text overlay without recompiling
2. trimClip places -ss BEFORE -i (fast seek) — is this correct? Any keyframe accuracy concerns?
3. No video stabilization — need to implement 'operation: stabilize' using vidstab or an alternative
4. h264_videotoolbox used everywhere (macOS hardware encoder only) — need a cross-platform encoder strategy
5. Any other issues you spot in the code

For each issue, provide the corrected TypeScript/ffmpeg code we should use.
